  "notes": "West leads the ♥Q against 4♠. West's heart opening lead holds. West shifts to a trump and South draws a second round. It looks like the ♦Q, ♣K, and ♣Q will all have to be offside for the contract to fail.\n\nSouth can make the contract even if all three finesses are wrong by playing for an elimination. South should cash the top diamonds and, when the ♦Q is still out, exit a third round.\n\nIf West wins the ♦Q and exits a club (he should have switched to a club at trick 2), South ducks in dummy. East can win, but he will be endplayed. A club return, will pick up the suit for 1 loser. A heart return will yield a ruff and discard.\n\nIf West has a diamond to return South can win in hand and pass a club to East, enplaying him as before. If East wins the third round of diamonds, his only safe exit will be in diamonds. South can win that trick and pass a club to East. Once again, East will be endplayed.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥Q against 4♠. West's heart opening lead holds. West shifts to a trump and South draws a second round. It looks like the ♦Q, ♣K, and ♣Q will all have to be offside for the contract to fail.",
    "South can make the contract even if all three finesses are wrong by playing for an elimination. South should cash the top diamonds and, when the ♦Q is still out, exit a third round.",
    "If West wins the ♦Q and exits a club (he should have switched to a club at trick 2), South ducks in dummy. East can win, but he will be endplayed. A club return, will pick up the suit for 1 loser. A heart return will yield a ruff and discard.",
    "If West has a diamond to return South can win in hand and pass a club to East, enplaying him as before. If East wins the third round of diamonds, his only safe exit will be in diamonds. South can win that trick and pass a club to East. Once again, East will be endplayed."
  ],
